{
  "_comment": "Used by the ci_infer CMake target (#5715 item 4b). fail-on-issue makes CI fail on Infer findings; disable-issue-type is a type-level baseline for the ~174 pre-existing findings (all PULSE_UNNECESSARY_COPY*/PULSE_RESOURCE_LEAK/PULSE_CONST_REFABLE, mostly in test code) triaged in run https://github.com/nlohmann/json/actions/runs/35829411620 on commit 1054b2097, so CI fails only on a NEW issue type. Remove an entry here once its findings have been fixed or explicitly accepted.",
  "_comment_pulse": "Pulse stops exploring paths after pulse-max-disjuncts (default 20). With the default, basic_json::replace_value() (destroy + assert_invariant) exceeds the limit, Pulse loses the stored type, and reports false NULLPTR_DEREFERENCE findings for get_ptr() results in tests/src/unit-pointer_access.cpp.",
  "_comment_view": "Infer's model of std::unique_ptr mixes up the `built` values that the helper build() in tests/src/unit-json_view_builder.cpp returns by value: it reports USE_AFTER_DELETE for one result after the destructor of an unrelated temporary (e.g. ~built() on line 345 invalidating `shallow` on line 350). AddressSanitizer is clean on the same tests, so reports for that test file are excluded; findings in the library headers it includes are still reported.",
  "pulse-max-disjuncts": 40,
  "fail-on-issue": true,
  "disable-issue-type": [
    "PULSE_UNNECESSARY_COPY_ASSIGNMENT",
    "PULSE_UNNECESSARY_COPY",
    "PULSE_UNNECESSARY_COPY_INTERMEDIATE",
    "PULSE_UNNECESSARY_COPY_OPTIONAL",
    "PULSE_RESOURCE_LEAK",
    "PULSE_CONST_REFABLE"
  ],
  "report-block-list-path-regex": [
    "tests/src/unit-json_view_builder\\.cpp"
  ]
}
